 "script": "An Xbox One can't install GTA 6. It's getting it on day one anyway. The trick: the game runs on Microsoft's servers and streams to your console through Xbox Cloud Gaming. Xbox Series X and S install it natively. Pre-loading takes up to 212 gigabytes. Pre-load opened November 10th. Cloud playtime went on sale the 11th, in supported markets, no Game Pass needed. Streaming starts at 1 a.m. Eastern on November 19th. The catch: it streams at Xbox Series S graphics settings, and the game still has to be bought separately. Would you stream GTA 6 on an Xbox One? Comment below.",
